+### Import tickets: `POST /tickets/import`
+
+Send `{ "tickets": [...] }` with at most 5000 items, each using the fields of `POST /tickets`.
+The service validates every item before creating any tickets. An invalid item returns 400 `invalid` with
+its zero-based index, for example `tickets[2]: title must not be empty`; the first invalid item is reported.
+No tickets, audit entries, notifications or ids are consumed when validation fails.
+
+Success returns 201 with `{ "created": 2, "ids": ["T-0001", "T-0002"] }`, in input order.
+An empty array succeeds with zero created tickets. Each ticket receives the ordinary creation audit entry
+and requester notification. The batch is saved once. Imports accept up to 10 MiB of JSON (or
+`MAX_BODY_BYTES` if larger); other endpoints retain `MAX_BODY_BYTES`.
+
 ### List tickets: `GET /tickets`
 
